      "windows95"
    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "The Soviet Union had ended, South Africa was negotiating change, and the US economy needed support. Job cuts and holiday products appeared side by side.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "Company share prices did not all follow the broad market. Owning many businesses reduced reliance on the fortunes of one retailer or entertainment company.",
    "what_faded_away": "The popularity of a particular holiday product did not predict an entire company’s five-year return. A rate cut was also only one part of the picture.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "No one could know the exact investment ranking. New political institutions and new products would take years to develop.",
